From 91d306c05fdde1c00d6ce07c01b0246d71fc28fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:57:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add a live-embed (iframe) block for case studies
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Projects can now carry a 'Sito live (iframe)' block in the execution
array alongside Testo and Media: an editable URL, height and heading,
rendered as an <iframe> with a fallback link that always sits next to
the frame rather than behind a failure this page cannot detect — a
site that refuses to be framed (X-Frame-Options / CSP) just renders an
empty box, with no error a script here can observe.

payload-types.ts updated by hand (LiveEmbedBlock / LiveEmbedBlockSelect,
both unions) rather than via 'generate:types', which needs a live DB
connection this environment doesn't have. Run generate:types once
against a real database to confirm it reproduces the same shape.
